---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Write a backup back into its board.
It replaces what is on the board now, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst backup restore <board> <key> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to write the backup into
  key     The backup's key from `holst backup ls`

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
  -y, --yes            Confirm a risky change; without it only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst backup restore "Roadmap" 1761552000 -y
  $ holst backup restore "Roadmap" 1761552000 -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
